==================================================================================================
PART A -- BASELINE: Jacobson gr-qc/9504004 reproduced symbolically (the validation anchor)
==================================================================================================
  A1. local balance with T = kappa/2pi  =>  T_kk = R_kk*eta/(2*pi)
   [A1 T_kk = (eta/2pi) R_kk, kappa cancels] PASS
      => R_kk = (2pi/eta) T_kk for all null k => Einstein eqs, G = 1/(4 eta),
         with Lambda entering ONLY as the Bianchi integration constant. [REPRODUCED]
  A2. explicit null k^mu=(1/f,1,0,0) in dS static patch: g_mn k^m k^n = 0
   [A2 g_kk = 0 (Lambda-term invisible to the balance)] PASS
  A3. d/dx(R/2 + f) = 0  =>  f = C1 - R(x)/2  (Lambda = the constant; NOT derived, NOT modified)
   [A3 f = -R/2 + const] PASS

==================================================================================================
PART B -- THE SUBSTRATE: exact dS worldline thermodynamics (full Christoffel computation)
==================================================================================================
  B1. u.u = -1;  a^mu = (0, -H**2*r, 0, 0);  |a|^2 = -H**4*r**2/(H**2*r**2 - 1)
   [B1 |a|^2 = (H^2 r)^2/(1-H^2 r^2)  [=> |a| = H^2 r/sqrt(1-H^2r^2)]] PASS
   [B2 a^2+H^2 = H^2/(1-H^2r^2)  [=> kappa_DL = H/sqrt(1-H^2r^2)]] PASS
  B3. (a^2+H^2) * |xi|^2 = H**2   [Deser-Levin = Tolman-shifted Gibbons-Hawking, EXACT]
   [B3 (T_DL*|xi|)^2 = (H/2pi)^2 exactly (kappa_b = H; positive => T_DL|xi| = H/2pi)] PASS
  B4. ell(r) = (-asin(H*r) + pi/2)/H  =>  r(ell) = cos(H ell)/H
      a(ell)^2 = H**2/tan(H*ell)**2  ;  kappa_DL(ell)^2 = H**2/sin(H*ell)**2
   [B4a a(ell)^2 = H^2 cot^2(H ell)  [=> a = H cot(H ell)]] PASS
   [B4b kappa_DL(ell)^2 = H^2/sin^2(H ell)  [=> kappa_DL = H/sin(H ell)]] PASS
      series  a*ell           = -H**4*ell**4/45 - H**2*ell**2/3 + 1
      series  kappa_DL*ell    = 7*H**4*ell**4/360 + H**2*ell**2/6 + 1
      series  sqrt(1+(Hell)^2)= -H**4*ell**4/8 + H**2*ell**2/2 + 1    [the flat-frame 'naive' DL]
   [B4c a*ell = 1 - (Hell)^2/3 - (Hell)^4/45] PASS
   [B4d kappa_DL*ell = 1 + (Hell)^2/6 + 7(Hell)^4/360] PASS
   [B4e naive = 1 + (Hell)^2/2 - (Hell)^4/8] PASS

==================================================================================================
PART C -- READING R1 (Tolman-consistent bookkeeping): the H^2 term propagates NOWHERE
==================================================================================================
  C1. (dE_loc/T_DL)^2 = (dQ_xi/|xi|)^2 / (kappa_DL/2pi)^2 = 4*pi**2*deltaQ_xi**2/H**2
   [C1 dE_loc/T_DL = 2pi dQ_xi / H  -- ell-free AND the H^2-in-quadrature is GONE] PASS
      With the EXACT Deser-Levin temperature the Clausius ratio collapses to the
      Killing-normalized Jacobson ratio 2pi*dQ_xi/kappa_b: identical balance, identical
      equation of state, at ALL orders in H/a. The sqrt(a^2+H^2) is nothing but the Tolman
      factor of the horizon temperature -- it cancels against the Tolman factor of the
      locally measured heat. Jacobson-with-DL = Jacobson, identically. Lambda is NOT
      re-derived (A3: still the integration constant); no MOND; no correction AT ANY ORDER.
==================================================================================================
PART D -- READING R2 (proper-frame DL at finite a: the ONLY reading where H survives)
==================================================================================================
  D1. balance  =>  T_kk = R_kk*eta*sqrt(H**2 + a**2)/(2*pi*a)   =>  G_eff/G = a/sqrt(H**2 + a**2)
   [D1 G_eff/G = a/sqrt(a^2+H^2)] PASS
   [D2a G_eff/G == mu_F4 = a/kappa (the F4 kernel, exactly)] PASS
   [D2b a/kappa == T_U^flat(a)/T_DL(a)] PASS
   [D2c a/kappa == 2pi * dT_DL/da  (F4's susceptibility, normalized)] PASS
      => The Clausius balance consumes T itself; F4 consumes dT/da. By the algebra of
         the quadrature they are the SAME function a/kappa -- but Clausius hangs it on G
         (the force side), F4 on m_eff (the inertia side).
  D3. G_eff/G = (1+x)^(-1/2), x=(H/a)^2  =  -5*x**3/16 + 3*x**2/8 - x/2 + 1  + O(x^4)
   [D3 coefficients 1, -1/2, +3/8, -5/16] PASS
   [D4 W = kappa_DL/a >= 1 for all (a,H>0)  [G_eff <= G: no temperature reading can flip it]] PASS
  D5. G_eff/G = a/sqrt(a^2+(cH)^2)   [Z = sqrt(32pi/3) = 5.7888]
          a/cH    G_eff/G   regime
           100     1.0000   Newtonian
             3     0.9487   transition
             1     0.7071   transition
         0.173     0.1702   a = a0 (deep-MOND onset)
          0.03     0.0300   deep MOND: gravity ~gone
      at a = a0: G_eff/G = 1/sqrt(1+Z^2) = 0.17023  (footing-independent statement:
      pure-Lambda (H/a0)^2 = Z^2 = 33.51; rho_total footing (cH0/a0')^2 = 33.60 -- same regime)
  D6. force-side   a = mu(a) g_N  =>  solutions a = [sqrt(-H**2 + g_N**2)]
   [D6a force-side: a = sqrt(g_N^2 - H^2) -- REAL ONLY FOR g_N > cH; below: a = 0 (total shutoff)] PASS
      inertia-side mu(a) a = g_N  =>  a = [sqrt(g_N**2/2 - g_N*sqrt(4*H**2 + g_N**2)/2), sqrt(g_N**2/2 + g_N*sqrt(4*H**2 + g_N**2)/2)]
   [D6b physical root present in solve()] PASS
   [D6c inertia-side deep-MOND limit: a^2/(g_N H) -> 1, i.e. a -> sqrt(g_N H) (the MOND enhancement)] PASS
      SAME function, two legs: on the INERTIA leg a/kappa gives deep-MOND a = sqrt(g_N H)
      (enhancement -- the observed phenomenology, F4's selling point); on the GRAVITY leg the
      Clausius balance puts it, the self-consistent response below g_N = cH is a = 0 EXACTLY:
      gravity does not weaken gradually -- it SHUTS OFF. Anti-MOND in its most extreme form
      (the banked sign, now exact and structural).
