PART E -- OUTCOME (i) TEST: the correction is NOT a cosmological-constant term
==================================================================================================
  E1. correction term = 8 pi G (mu_F4 - 1) T_kk = 8*pi*G*T_kk*a/sqrt(H**2 + a**2) - 8*pi*G*T_kk
      proportional to T_kk (a SOURCE-coupling rescaling), NOT to g_kk (which is 0, A2).
   [E1 correction vanishes when T_kk = 0 (so it can NEVER mimic Lambda, which gravitates in vacuum)] PASS
      Lambda remains exactly where Jacobson left it: the Bianchi integration constant (A3),
      untouched by the temperature substitution. Outcome (i) does NOT occur.
